## Appending a helper

To insert helper code without overwriting any existing function, anchor on the file's CURRENT last line:

- Set `start_line` = `end_line` = L (the file's current last line number)
- Set `old_block` = the exact current text of line L (use `file_editor view` to read it if unsure)
- Set `new_block` = `<old_block>` + `\n\n` + `<helper source>`

Each helper insert grows the file by N lines, so update `L = L + N` before the next insert (or just `view` again).

This is the safe pattern. Setting `start_line`/`end_line` to "the line immediately after the original function" overwrites whatever happens to be there and is forbidden — it is what produced structurally-broken files in past runs.

